-- title:
--   Root-group and cycle-response evaluation programs
-- statement:
--   These programs evaluate ordinary and primary root-group contributions, cycle-touch information, cycle ranks and averages, signed masses, packed roots, and root metadata. They compute the selected finite response used to assemble the full calibration matrix while retaining the exact decoded mathematical interpretation.
-- source:
--   Companion Lean implementation for the fixed-family Gaussian affine transport theorem. The source modules and their SHA-256 hashes are recorded in the checked extraction manifest. This exact generated file has SHA-256 da04c8cb873ec84908ec95e74925d831214a9d4d5f9aa41e4cb1610851241e43. Source modules: Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootGroupOrdinary, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootGroupLegMass, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootGroupPrimary, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootGroupLeg, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootGroup, Integration9_9_TM2NativeCycleTouched, Integration9_9_TM2NativeCycleRanks, Integration9_9_TM2NativeCycleEvaluation, Integration9_9_TM2NativeCycleAverage, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootSignedMass, Integration9_9_TM2NativeWeightedPoint, Integration9_9_TM2NativePackedRoot, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootMetadata, Integration9_9_TM2NativeMetadataDispatch, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRootTags, Integration9_9_TM2NativeSelectedResponse. Alternate sparse native dependencies preserve the original non-import body bytes and all public types; this header-only packaging is recorded in sparse_live/manifest.json. Current source SHA256 28b4dfecc5ef2f1661618f301f8bc4d2b3822982a9be70e0bc486ede3b2fcff9. Native10/11 split fallback keeps every original scope-closed data body unchanged and retains the canonical module names as import facades. Current source SHA256 28b4dfecc5ef2f1661618f301f8bc4d2b3822982a9be70e0bc486ede3b2fcff9.

